      "preprocess": {
        "layout": "NCHW",
        "color": "RGB",
        "resize": "face bbox expanded by expand_bbox(factor=0.2) then resized to 224x224",
        "formula": "((pixel_rgb / 255) - mean) / std",
        "mean": [
          0.485,
          0.456,
          0.406
        ],
        "std": [
          0.229,
          0.224,
          0.225
        ],
        "source": "detect.py pre_process(): cvtColor BGR2RGB, Resize(224), ToTensor, Normalize(ImageNet)"
      },
      "postprocess": "Output is a full 3x3 rotation matrix R (the 6D ortho representation is already converted inside the graph). Euler, in radians, per utils/general.py compute_euler_angles_from_rotation_matrices: sy = sqrt(R[0,0]^2 + R[1,0]^2); if sy >= 1e-6: pitch = atan2(R[2,1], R[2,2]), yaw = atan2(-R[2,0], sy), roll = atan2(R[1,0], R[0,0]); else pitch = atan2(-R[1,2], R[1,1]), yaw = atan2(-R[2,0], sy), roll = 0. Upstream prints euler[:,0] as pitch, euler[:,1] as yaw, euler[:,2] as roll, in degrees."
    },
