      },
      "postprocess": "Both outputs are 90-bin LOGITS (no softmax in the graph). bins=90, binwidth=4, angle_offset=180 (gaze360 config). deg = sum(softmax(logits) * arange(90)) * 4 - 180, then radians(deg). Output order is (yaw, pitch): yaw = horizontal, pitch = vertical, both relative to the face crop."
    },
    "objects": {
      "id": "yolox_nano",
      "file": "yolox_nano.onnx",
      "url": "https://github.com/Megvii-BaseDetection/YOLOX/releases/download/0.1.1rc0/yolox_nano.onnx",
      "sha256": "c789161ed43c8269fcd4e67c67eeeb4e80c622da2eb296a20bc6007bd18a0b7d",
      "bytes": 3659407,
      "license": "Apache-2.0 (Megvii-BaseDetection/YOLOX). COCO-trained. This replaces the AGPL-3.0 Ultralytics YOLOv8n plan - no licence acceptance required.",
      "cookbook": "https://github.com/Megvii-BaseDetection/YOLOX",
      "input_name": "images",
      "input_shape": [
        1,
        3,
        416,
        416
      ],
      "input_dtype": "FLOAT",
      "output_names": [
        "output"
      ],
      "output_shapes": {
        "output": [
          1,
          3549,
          85
        ]
      },
      "preprocess": {
        "layout": "NCHW",
        "color": "BGR",
        "resize": "letterbox: r = min(416/h, 416/w); resize to (round down w*r, h*r) INTER_LINEAR into a 416x416 canvas prefilled with 114, anchored TOP-LEFT (no centring)",
        "formula": "pixel_bgr (raw 0-255, NO /255, NO mean, NO std)",
        "mean": [
          0.0,
          0.0,
          0.0
        ],
        "std": [
          1.0,
          1.0,
          1.0
        ],
        "source": "yolox/data/data_augment.py preproc(); demo/ONNXRuntime/onnx_inference.py"
      },
      "postprocess": "3549 = 52*52 + 26*26 + 13*13, strides 8/16/32 concatenated in that order. Per row: [dx, dy, dw, dh, obj, cls_0..cls_79]. obj and cls are ALREADY sigmoid-activated inside the graph; the grid decode is NOT: cx = (dx + grid_x) * stride, cy = (dy + grid_y) * stride, w = exp(dw) * stride, h = exp(dh) * stride, in 416-space. score = obj * cls_i. Convert to xyxy, divide by the letterbox ratio r to get source-image pixels, then class-wise NMS (upstream nms_thr 0.45, score_thr 0.1). COCO-80 class order; 'cell phone' = index 67, 'bottle' = 39, 'cup' = 41, 'person' = 0.",
      "verification": "grid decode confirmed NOT baked in and obj/cls confirmed sigmoid-activated by running the built engine on a real frame - see engines/yolox_nano_416_fp16_gpu.engine.build.log and the semantics probe recorded in engines[objects].output_semantics_probe."
    },
